00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:01.720
happening physiologically. Emotional

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:04.120
tears contain cortisol and other stress

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:06.400
hormones that your body is literally

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:07.640
flushing out through the tear duct. Dr.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:09.199
William Frey of the University of

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:10.680
Minnesota published research on this

00:17:09.199 --> 00:17:12.439
showing that emotional tears have a

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:14.439
completely different chemical

00:17:12.439 --> 00:17:16.920
composition than reflex tears. They

00:17:14.439 --> 00:17:19.040
contain stress hormones, mood-regulating

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:21.240
neurotransmitters. All that tension in

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:23.800
your body gets released. So, after a

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:26.400
real cry, your whole body can actually

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:27.920
calm down. I used to pride myself on

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:30.120
